course: dictionary
lesson: 11386
title: The word abundance
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abundance means a very large amount of something, more than enough. When there is an abundance of something, there is plenty of it. «The farm had an abundance of apples this year.» The words around it tell you the farm had more apples than it needed.
explain: Look for the phrases it often sits in: «an abundance of», «in abundance» and «abundance of food». In «Wildflowers grew in abundance along the river», the words grew in abundance tell you the flowers were everywhere, not just a few here and there.
explain: Abundance is often the opposite of a famine, a time when there is not enough food. «After the good rains, the fields were full of corn, and the village had an abundance of food.» Swap in the word plenty and check: the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Abundance is a noun. It names the state of having plenty, or a very large amount of something.
fact: You will often see it in the phrases «an abundance of», «in abundance» and «abundance of food».
fact: Scientists use it for nature: «The lake had an abundance of fish, so the herons were never hungry.»
fact: In stories, abundance often paints a picture of riches and plenty, the opposite of famine.
fact: Abundance is a big, rich word. Use it when you mean much more than just a little.
exercise: «The forest had an abundance of mushrooms after the rain.» What does abundance mean here? | *Plenty, more than enough | A kind of tree | Very dark and quiet | A long walk
exercise: «Wildflowers grew in abundance on the hill.» What does «in abundance» mean here? | *In great numbers, everywhere | Only just | In a box, hidden away | Very slowly, one at a time
exercise: Ravi says abundance means a very small amount. Is he right? | Yes, it means empty | No, it means a loud noise | Yes, it means a tiny bit | *No, it means a very large amount, more than enough
test: Which word is the opposite of abundance? | Feast | *Famine | Harvest | Plenty
test: Which phrase means the same as «abundance of food»? | No food at all | A shortage of food | *Plenty of food | Cold food
exam: «The village had an abundance of water after the storm.» Which word could you swap in for abundance and keep the same meaning? | Shortage | Silence | *Plenty | Danger
